      "found_by": null,
      "deleted": null,
      "references": "- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-18149\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/3c6726599cea8646384dde846c97d630da472a74\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/e905b5b87e6953bcc542af90557b2fee5b7b5974\n- https://hackerone.com/reports/3892751\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.29.1\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.10.2\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x",
      "created": "2026-09-29T18:22:34.000Z",
      "id": 1240036,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\nundici's `RetryHandler` can leave a response body pending indefinitely. When a retried request receives a non-retryable response after a truncated one, the original `response.body` held by the application is never settled, so reads such as `response.body.text()` hang and `bodyTimeout` does not fire. A malicious server can repeat this to accumulate pending promises and streams, leading to denial of service.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatched in undici v7.29.1 and v8.10.2.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nImpose an independent request deadline and destroy the response body when it expires. `bodyTimeout` alone does not prevent this.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "undici vulnerable to Denial of Service via orphaned RetryHandler response body",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-18149"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "module_name": "undici",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=7.11.0 <7.29.1",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 7.29.1 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=7.29.1",
      "updated": "2026-09-29T18:22:35.000Z",
      "cvss": {
        "score": 5.9,
        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
      },
